<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Glance</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>glance &lt;someone&gt;
</pre>
<p>A thief's discreet look at someone: their description and what they 
wear, without them seeing you look. A plain <a cmd='#'>Help Look</a> tells them you 
looked at them; a glance doesn't, unless it fails.
</p><p>You must be sneaking and hidden first (see <a cmd='#'>Help Sneak</a> and <a cmd='#'>Help 
Hide</a>). Your dexterity and brains are set against theirs:
</p>
<ul><li>a good glance shows everything they wear, and whether they have signed the Book of Blood;</li>
<li>a fair one shows only some of it;</li>
<li>a failed one, and they catch you at it and slap you in the face.</li></ul>
<p>The Thieves of Udgaard teach glance from guild level 9, and the 
Assassins from guild level 5.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Peeking</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Sneak</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Hide</a>
</pre>




</div>